================================================================================
NO WARRANTY, AND A LIMIT ON WHAT THIS TOOL IS FOR
================================================================================

Provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. Built to teach relationships and
orders of magnitude: where the sun is, what falls in shadow, and roughly how
much radiation a surface collects over a day or a year.

It is NOT validated for regulatory or compliance work. The shadows you see are a
GPU shadow map and the numbers you get are a ray test against a bounding-volume
hierarchy — two different machineries that can disagree at the edges. Reflected
light is not modelled at all: every surface is treated as fully absorbing, so an
urban courtyard reads darker than it is. Read docs/method-notes.html, which
states every assumption the code makes and declares what it leaves out.

For a compliance submission, an energy model, or any figure a consultant will
stake a fee on, use Radiance through Ladybug and Honeybee, IESVE, or an
equivalent validated tool.


